    <div class="dropdown-divider"></div>
    <a class="dropdown-item text-danger" ...><i class="fa fa-trash mr-2"></i>Delete</a>
  </div>
</div>
```
But inside a `.table-responsive` with DataTables, dropdown menus may be clipped by overflow. Common issue: `.table-responsive { overflow-x: auto; }` clips dropdown. In Bootstrap 4, dropdown open inside overflow container gets clipped vertically. Solutions:
- Add CSS to allow `.table-responsive` overflow visible? That breaks horizontal scroll on small screens.
- Use `data-container="body"`? That's Bootstrap 3 tooltip.
- Use DataTables' responsive? Not loaded responsive extension.
- Implement custom popup menu using absolutely positioned menu with JS appended to body (floating). More code.
- Simpler: use a `<details>` element? Also clipped.
- Use a custom JS menu appended to body positioned at button. That's robust.

But simplest acceptable: make the dropdown menu open upward and allow table-responsive overflow visible on desktop (only horizontal scroll needed on mobile). Could set `.products-table-wrap { overflow: visible; }` on >= lg, and default auto under md. Dropdown last row would still be clipped on mobile but table scrolls. Hmm.

Alternatively use Bootstrap's `dropdown-menu` with CSS `.table-responsive { overflow: visible; }` globally at min-width 768. Given many products and page scrolling, open downward may extend beyond viewport bottom at last rows but page can scroll.

Better approach: implement a small custom action menu with a fixed-position panel appended to `document.body`, positioned relative to the trigger using getBoundingClientRect. Handles clipping and viewport edges. Also outside click closes, Escape closes, scroll closes. This is a bit more JS but reliable.

However project already uses Bootstrap; a dropdown with `data-boundary="window"` (Bootstrap 4.3+ supports Popper boundary) might escape overflow? Popper's boundary option constrains within scroll parent; by default Popper has `boundary: 'scrollParent'`, which is the overflow container → clipped. Setting `data-boundary="viewport"`? Bootstrap 4 doesn't expose boundary via data attribute except `data-reference`, `data-offset`, `data-display`. Hmm.

