Then JS moves it to body? Simpler: CSS `position: fixed` menu positioned via JS with left/top. Keep menu inside cell, but `position: fixed` escapes overflow clipping of ancestors (fixed is relative to viewport, not clipped by overflow ancestors... actually overflow clipping does not apply to position:fixed unless an ancestor has transform/filter/will-change). The table-responsive has no transform. So `position: fixed` menu works inside overflow container without clipping. 

