Let me first fix the helpers function (done) and verify no breakage. Then implement authentication.

User::authenticate update.

Let's edit User.php with fallback matching. Need to be careful with `new self()` hydration. Implement private static `hydrate($row)`.

Current authenticate:
```php
$stmt = prepare SELECT * WHERE (username=? OR email=?) AND is_active=1
...
if (!$row || !password_verify(...)) return null;
$user = new self(); copy; loadRoles; update last_login; return.
```
Rewrite:

```php
public static function authenticate($identifier, $password) {
    global $conn;
    $identifier = trim((string)$identifier);
    if ($identifier === '' || $password === '') return null;

    $candidates = [];
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("SELECT * FROM users WHERE (username = ? OR email = ?) AND is_active = 1 LIMIT 5");
    $stmt->bind_param('ss', $identifier, $identifier);
    $stmt->execute(); $res = ...; while rows candidates[]; close.

    if (!$candidates) {
        $norm = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9]/i', '', mb_strtolower($identifier));
        $digits = preg_replace('/\D+/', '', $identifier);
        $rows = fetch_all("SELECT * FROM users WHERE is_active = 1");
        foreach ($rows as $row) {
            $phone_digits = preg_replace('/\D+/', '', (string)($row['phone'] ?? ''));
            $username_norm = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9]/i', '', mb_strtolower((string)$row['username']));
            $full_name = trim(($row['first_name'] ?? '') . ' ' . ($row['last_name'] ?? ''));
            $name_norm = preg_replace('/[^a-z0-9]/i', '', mb_strtolower($full_name));
            $phone_match = $digits !== '' && strlen($digits) >= 7 && $phone_digits !== '' && (str_ends_with($phone_digits, $digits) || str_ends_with($digits, $phone_digits));
            $name_match = $norm !== '' && ($norm === $username_norm || $norm === $name_norm);
            if ($phone_match || $name_match) $candidates[] = $row;
        }
    }

    foreach ($candidates as $row) {
        if (!password_verify($password, $row['password_hash'])) continue;
        $user = self::fromRow($row);
        update last_login;
        return $user;
    }
    return null;
}
```
`str_ends_with` PHP 8+ (project PHP 8.2). But phone suffix: if typed "0712345678" (10 digits) and stored "+255712345678" (12), last 9 digits both "712345678". `str_ends_with($phone_digits,$digits)` false if digits longer; `str_ends_with($digits,$phone_digits)` false. Use compare last 9:
```php
$tail = fn($d) => strlen($d) > 9 ? substr($d, -9) : $d;
$phone_match = strlen($digits)>=7 && strlen($phone_digits)>=7 && $tail($digits) === $tail($phone_digits);
```
Good.

Also avoid fetching all users including staff on every failed login — fine for small app, but could be heavy. Limit to users with phone or wholesaler role? Could restrict to active users with phone non-null OR role wholesaler. Name login applies to staff too; but requirement only wholesalers. Simpler restrict fallback to users with phone not null (staff have phones maybe) OR wholesaler role via subquery:
```sql
SELECT * FROM users WHERE is_active=1 AND (phone IS NOT NULL AND phone <> '' OR EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM user_roles ur JOIN roles r ... LOWER(r.name)='wholesaler'))
```
Good enough. Or just all.

Implement helper `fromRow` to avoid duplication. Add private static function.

