content.text:
We need modify product card bottom: use #BE2430 background, description text white/visible.

Which "bottom"? Product card body? They say "product card botton use BE2430 as background then the descriptions be white or any color visible". Likely the bottom section of product card (name/price area) should have red background with white text. We previously added red top border and red price. Now wants bottom area background red, description (product name/price) white.

Product card markup has `.sf-product-body` containing name and meta (price). "descriptions" maybe product description; current card shows only name, meta in storefront_render_product_card (no description). Actually card body only h3 name + meta price. Maybe they call that description. Set `.sf-product-body { background: #BE2430; border-top... }`; `.sf-product-body h3, .sf-product-body h3 a, .sf-price, .sf-price-compare, .sf-unit { color: #fff; }`; meta border white translucent; hover no red change. This is bold but requested.

But this applies all product cards. "bottom" maybe only the lower strip (price) not entire body. Could set `.sf-product-meta { background: #BE2430; color:#fff; margin: 10px -14px -14px; padding: 10px 14px; border-top:none; }` so bottom strip red with white price. "descriptions be white" maybe the name? If only price strip, description (name) dark. They say "then the descriptions be white" suggests whole bottom section including name/description gets red background and white text. Let's set the product body (bottom section) red with white name/price. That matches "product card bottom".

Modify CSS:
```css
.sf-product-body { background: var(--sf-accent); border-top: 0; color:#fff; }
.sf-product-body h3 { color:#fff; }
.sf-product-body h3 a { color:#fff; }
.sf-product-meta { border-top-color: rgba(255,255,255,.35); }
