content.text:
Now viewport is 800x620, so the search wraps. The non-active tabs have color rgb(28,36,48) = --sf-text, not our rgba white. Why? Something overrides `.sf-tab` color. Likely `.sf-body a { color: inherit; }` is more specific? `.sf-body a` specificity 0,1,1 vs `.sf-tab` 0,1,0. So `.sf-body a` wins and sets color inherit (from body = #1c2430). Need a more specific selector, e.g., `.sf-body .sf-tab { color: rgba(255,255,255,.82); }` or `.sf-tabs .sf-tab`. Same for hover and active? Active has `.sf-tab[aria-current="page"]` specificity 0,2,0 vs `.sf-body a` 0,1,1; active wins (0,2,0 > 0,1,1? compare specificity: (0,2,0) vs (0,1,1): second component 2 > 1, so active wins). That's why active is white. Hover `.sf-tab:hover` (0,2,0) wins. So only base needs specificity. Add `.sf-body .sf-tab { color: rgba(...) }` and `.sf-body .sf-tab i`. Or use `.sf-tabs .sf-tab`.

Let's update the CSS:
```css
.sf-tabs .sf-tab { color: rgba(255,255,255,.82); }
.sf-tabs .sf-tab i { color: rgba(255,255,255,.66); }
.sf-tabs .sf-tab:hover { color:#fff; }
.sf-tabs .sf-tab[aria-current="page"] { color:#fff; }
```
Simpler: change selectors to `.sf-body .sf-tab` for base and icon. Let's edit.

