...
.sf-search-wrap { flex-basis: 240px; min-width: 140px; }
```
With grid, `flex-basis` irrelevant; `min-width:140px` on search is okay, but grid column min 220 handles. `.sf-brand min-width:180` maybe conflicts with grid col min 220; min-width on grid item can stretch column. Set `max-width: 320px;` and remove min-width? Let's adjust:
- At 1100: `.sf-header-inner { gap:14px; grid-template-columns: minmax(180px, 300px) minmax(220px, 1fr) auto; }`, `.sf-brand { min-width:0; }`, `.sf-search-wrap { min-width:0; }`.

Maybe simpler: define grid base and at 1100 override columns. At 900 same as 1100. Let's do.

Also `.sf-brand-text strong max-width:460` but grid column max 420; the strong can overflow? The grid item width is max 420; the text overflows hidden. `.sf-brand` has min-width 0? Set `.sf-brand { min-width:0; }` so it can shrink. The strong max-width 460 but parent smaller; `overflow:hidden; text-overflow:ellipsis` with `white-space:nowrap` will truncate at parent width. Good.

