At 800:
- Header grid columns: brand 260, search 318, actions 135; brand x=24, search x=296, actions x=626. That's left/middle/right. Good.
- Filters below tabs: false. Good.
- Hero background image loaded. Good.
- Category cards 2, arrivals 3 (only 3 products available). Max 5 logic works (2 categories, 3 products). Category grid columns at 800: because media 900 doesn't override category grid? At 800 <=900 but >767, the 1100 media sets `.sf-category-grid { repeat(4) }`. So 4 columns with 2 cards. The `sf-category-grid--home` auto-fit is overridden by the media (4 columns). That's fine, but 2 cards occupy 2 of 4 columns, leaving 2 empty. At this viewport, category cards are 173px wide, small. Hmm. The user wants up to 5 items; with 2 categories, 4 columns leaves empty space. Could improve by making the home category grid use auto-fit at all widths until 767. Our `sf-category-grid--home` is overridden by `.sf-category-grid` at 1100/767 due to same specificity. We can increase specificity to `.sf-category-grid.sf-category-grid--home` so it stays auto-fit at 1100 and 900; but at 767 we want 2 columns. Add:
```css
.sf-category-grid.sf-category-grid--home { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); }
@media (max-width: 767px) { .sf-category-grid.sf-category-grid--home { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); } }
```
At 800, auto-fit min 220 with 752px content: 3 columns (3*220+2*16=692) → 3 columns, 2 items → 2 of 3, still empty. At 1240, 5 columns. Hmm. To fill with 2 items, auto-fit with 2 items creates as many tracks as items? `auto-fit` collapses empty tracks and stretches items to fill: with 2 items, it creates 2 tracks that stretch to fill the container. Actually `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px,1fr))` creates up to floor((width+gap)/(220+gap)) tracks, but empty tracks collapse, and the items stretch to fill available space. With 2 items, only 2 tracks remain and they stretch to half width each. So at 800, 2 cards would each be ~368px. That's better. Our current 4-column grid gives 2 small cards. So specificity fix is worth it.

Let's change `.sf-category-grid--home` to `.sf-category-grid.sf-category-grid--home` (0,2,0) and add a 767 override (0,2,0) inside media. Then at 1100 media `.sf-category-grid` (0,1,0) won't override. At 767, existing `.sf-category-grid` repeat(2) (0,1,0) won't override the compound; add explicit:
```css
@media (max-width: 767px) { .sf-category-grid.sf-category-grid--home { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); } }
```
At 420, maybe 1 column? Existing 420 only changes product grid, not category grid. 2 columns on tiny screens may be okay for category tiles; existing behavior was 2 columns at 767. Keep 2.

